{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773093585,"nonce":"TAue2V66SptPeg7GbmzZjwwk+ss=","title":"Issues view: label pills and status pills visually indistinct; \"error\" label looks like error state","message":"Two confusion points reported:\n\n1. The \"error\" git-bug label (used for bug-fix issues) shows as an \"error\" pill in the issue detail, which looks like an error state indicator rather than a classification label.\n\n2. The \"merged\" status pill appears on issues in the issues view but provides no branch/repo context — users cannot tell where/when the issue was merged.\n\nFixes:\n- Display \"error\" label as \"bug\" in the UI (visual rename only, label stored as \"error\")\n- Consider adding a small visual prefix (e.g., tag icon) to label pills to distinguish them from the status pill\n- For \"merged\" issues, consider showing the branch name if available from git-bug metadata\n\nLabels: error, feature","files":null}]}